    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_THELIVINGWORLD_MCQ_Q02 - Taxonomic classification of mango and wheat</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Study the given taxonomic classification diagram comparing Mango (<em>Mangifera indica</em>) and Wheat (<em>Triticum aestivum</em>).</p><p><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 640 340" width="640" height="340" role="img" aria-label="Taxonomic classification tree for Mango and Wheat with missing labels X, Y, and Z"><rect x="0" y="0" width="640" height="340" fill="#ffffff"/><rect x="220" y="16" width="200" height="36" rx="6" fill="#e8f4f8" stroke="#2c6b8e" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="320" y="39" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a3c4d">Division: Angiospermae</text><line x1="320" y1="52" x2="320" y2="72" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="160" y1="72" x2="480" y2="72" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="160" y1="72" x2="160" y2="90" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="480" y1="72" x2="480" y2="90" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="65" y="90" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#fff7e6" stroke="#b37400" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="160" y="113" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#664200">Class: X</text><rect x="385" y="90" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#f0f8e8" stroke="#4c7a1a" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="480" y="113" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#2c4a0d">Class: Monocotyledonae</text><line x1="160" y1="126" x2="160" y2="148" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="480" y1="126" x2="480" y2="148" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="65" y="148" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#f9f9f9" stroke="#555555" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="160" y="171" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" fill="#222222">Order: Sapindales</text><rect x="385" y="148" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#fff7e6" stroke="#b37400" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="480" y="171" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#664200">Order: Z</text><line x1="160" y1="184" x2="160" y2="206" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="480" y1="184" x2="480" y2="206" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="65" y="206" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#fff7e6" stroke="#b37400" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="160" y="229" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#664200">Family: Y</text><rect x="385" y="206" width="190" height="36" rx="6" fill="#f9f9f9" stroke="#555555" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="480" y="229" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" fill="#222222">Family: Poaceae</text><line x1="160" y1="242" x2="160" y2="264" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><line x1="480" y1="242" x2="480" y2="264" stroke="#444444" stroke-width="1.5"/><rect x="55" y="264" width="210" height="44" rx="6" fill="#eef2f7" stroke="#335577" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="160" y="283" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-style="italic" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a2e40">Mangifera indica</text><text x="160" y="300" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#444444">(Mango)</text><rect x="375" y="264" width="210" height="44" rx="6" fill="#eef2f7" stroke="#335577" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="480" y="283" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-style="italic" font-weight="bold" text-anchor="middle" fill="#1a2e40">Triticum aestivum</text><text x="480" y="300" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" fill="#444444">(Wheat)</text></svg></p><p>Identify the missing taxonomic categories labelled <strong>X</strong>, <strong>Y</strong>, and <strong>Z</strong>.</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Conceptual Principle</strong><br/>Each plant species is placed in a hierarchical set of taxonomic categories: Species, Genus, Family, Order, Class, Division, and Kingdom.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Identification of X and Y (Mango)</strong><br/><em>Mangifera indica</em> (mango) belongs to the genus <em>Mangifera</em>, family Anacardiaceae, order Sapindales, class Dicotyledonae, and division Angiospermae. Therefore, the missing class <strong>X</strong> is Dicotyledonae, and the missing family <strong>Y</strong> is Anacardiaceae.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Identification of Z (Wheat)</strong><br/><em>Triticum aestivum</em> (wheat) belongs to the genus <em>Triticum</em>, family Poaceae, order Poales, class Monocotyledonae, and division Angiospermae. Therefore, the missing order <strong>Z</strong> is Poales.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The missing taxonomic categories are <strong>X</strong> = Dicotyledonae, <strong>Y</strong> = Anacardiaceae, and <strong>Z</strong> = Poales.</p>]]></text></generalfeedback>
